{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum spanning arborescence rooted at "},{"code":"root","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", by Edmonds’ algorithm; nil unless "},{"code":"root","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reaches every vertex."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/minimumspanningarborescence(from:weight:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumSpanningArborescence","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"root","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Branching","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees9BranchingV","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/Branching"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">? ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdditiveArithmetic","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"name":"root","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertex every edge points away from."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"weight","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each edge’s weight, from its position."}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The arborescence’s edges, in position order, and their total weight; nil when a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex cannot be reached from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"root"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The arborescence has one edge into every vertex but "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"root"},{"type":"text","text":", all of them pointing away from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, and the least total weight of any such set. Among equal-weight optima, which one is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returned is unspecified, but the same input always gives the same answer. Edges into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"root"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and self-loops are never weighed; every other edge is weighed once. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" is not kept."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The algorithm is Chu–Liu\/Edmonds with Tarjan’s contraction over mergeable heaps (skew heaps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with lazy offsets) and a union–find with rollback to expand the contracted cycles."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Negative and zero weights are ordinary weights."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(m log m).","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"},{"style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"root","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a vertex; every weight is finite (not NaN or infinite); the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"differences between weights do not overflow.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/minimumSpanningArborescence(from:weight:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"SpanningTrees"}],"title":"minimumSpanningArborescence(from:weight:)","symbolKind":"method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Edmonds.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpanningTrees\/Edmonds.swift#L25"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P13SpanningTreesE07minimumD12Arborescence4from6weightAD9BranchingVyxqd__GSg6VertexQz_qd__5Edges_5IndexQZXEts18AdditiveArithmeticRd__SLRd__lF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"}